# CodeBuddy project context

The canonical project-document entry is:
`documentation/codebuddy/CURRENT.md`

When the user asks about project status, current problems, progress, or planning:
1. Read `documentation/codebuddy/CURRENT.md` first.
2. Follow only the exact relative paths recorded there.
3. Inspect the current Git worktree and run relevant read-only checks before drawing conclusions.
4. Treat dates and test results in documents as historical evidence until verified on the current HEAD.

Do not infer a document path from its title, date, or basename. If `read_document` reports
`path_not_found`, stop guessing and use `tree` on the nearest existing directory. If multiple
plausible files remain, ask the user which one is intended.
